    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448">

                <pb facs="0524" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg358"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1091</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-15T12:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1917, noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Military conditions unchanged. Government troops to-day were in touch with forces
                    under Gómez near line between Santa Clara and Camaguey Provinces but are
                    awaiting arrival of regiment sent by sea from Habana before attacking.</p>
                <pb facs="0525" n="359" xml:id="pg359"/>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Petrel</hi> of naval station is at Santiago. Consul
                    there again reports conditions growing worse but no details.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
